IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: ss 76F and 76G -- payments for the acquisition of its own shares are made only if the company is solvent;
-- the reduction of capital or profits on cancellation of repurchased shares.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Lines 8937-9049 of inputs/CoA1967.txt (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words, NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- Tags {F-..} point at the fork register and {MR-a}, {MR-b} at the marginal readings for a lawyer (NOTES.md).

§ `Section 76F: payments to be made only if the company is solvent`

-- (4): "a company is solvent if at the date of the payment mentioned in subsection (1) the following conditions are satisfied".
-- src:8987 | (4) For the purposes of this section, a company is solvent if at the
-- src:8988 | date of the payment mentioned in subsection (1) the following
-- src:8989 | conditions are satisfied:
-- src:8991 | (a) there is no ground on which the company could be found to
-- src:8992 | be unable to pay its debts;
-- src:8994 | (b) if —
-- src:8996 | (i) it is intended to commence winding up of the
-- src:8997 | company within the period of 12 months
-- src:8998 | immediately after the date of the payment, the
-- src:8999 | company will be able to pay its debts in full within
-- src:9000 | the period of 12 months after the date of
-- src:9001 | commencement of the winding up; or
-- src:9003 | (ii) it is not intended so to commence winding up, the
-- src:9004 | company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due
-- src:9005 | during the period of 12 months immediately after the
-- src:9006 | date of the payment;
-- src:9008 | (c) the value of the company’s assets is not less than the value
-- src:9009 | of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities) and will
-- src:9010 | not, after the proposed purchase, acquisition, variation or
-- src:9011 | release (as the case may be), become less than the value of
-- src:9012 | its liabilities (including contingent liabilities).
@ref s 76F(4) (src:8987-9012)
GIVEN `there is no ground on which the company could be found to be unable to pay its debts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is intended to commence winding up of the company within the period of 12 months immediately after the date of the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company will be able to pay its debts in full within the period of 12 months after the date of commencement of the winding up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due during the period of 12 months immediately after the date of the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the company's assets is not less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the company's assets will not, after the proposed purchase, acquisition, variation or release, become less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76F(4) the company is solvent` MEANS
    IF    `there is no ground on which the company could be found to be unable to pay its debts`
      AND (IF `it is intended to commence winding up of the company within the period of 12 months immediately after the date of the payment`
           THEN `the company will be able to pay its debts in full within the period of 12 months after the date of commencement of the winding up`
           ELSE `the company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due during the period of 12 months immediately after the date of the payment`)
      AND `the value of the company's assets is not less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)`
      AND `the value of the company's assets will not, after the proposed purchase, acquisition, variation or release, become less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company is solvent if at the date of the payment mentioned in subsection (1) the following conditions are satisfied" (a definition by an "if"; a failed "if" counts as the text's no, marginal reading (a)) {F-F1} {MR-a}

-- (1): the payment "may be made out of the company's capital or profits so long as the company is solvent".
-- src:8939 | 76F.—(1) A payment made by a company in consideration of —
-- src:8941 | (a) acquiring any right with respect to the purchase or
-- src:8942 | acquisition of its own shares in accordance with
-- src:8943 | section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E;
-- src:8945 | (b) the variation of an agreement approved under section 76D
-- src:8946 | or 76DA; or
-- src:8948 | (c) the release of any of the company’s obligations with
-- src:8949 | respect to the purchase or acquisition of any of its own
-- src:8950 | shares under an agreement approved under section 76D or
-- src:8951 | 76DA,
-- src:8953 | may be made out of the company’s capital or profits so long as the
-- src:8954 | company is solvent.
@ref s 76F(1) (src:8939-8954)
GIVEN `the payment is made in consideration of acquiring a right with respect to the purchase or acquisition of the company's own shares in accordance with section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is made in consideration of the variation of an agreement approved under section 76D or 76DA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is made in consideration of the release of any of the company's obligations with respect to the purchase or acquisition of any of its own shares under an agreement approved under section 76D or 76DA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is solvent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76F(1) the payment may be made out of the company's capital or profits` MEANS
    IF NOT (   `the payment is made in consideration of acquiring a right with respect to the purchase or acquisition of the company's own shares in accordance with section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E`
            OR `the payment is made in consideration of the variation of an agreement approved under section 76D or 76DA`
            OR `the payment is made in consideration of the release of any of the company's obligations with respect to the purchase or acquisition of any of its own shares under an agreement approved under section 76D or 76DA`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A payment made by a company in consideration of (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..." names three kinds of payment; a payment of another kind is outside the subsection {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF `the company is solvent`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be made out of the company's capital or profits so long as the company is solvent" ("so long as" closes the gate; a "may" gated by a condition word, split site (ii), the periods ruling of 2026-11-05 item (b) read with item (c)) {F-F2} {MR-a}

