-- (3): the offence. "Every director or chief executive officer of a company who approves or authorises, the purchase or acquisition of the company's own shares or the release of obligations, knowing that the company is not solvent".
-- The text gives a fine "or" imprisonment (no "or to both"), so both is FALSE (fork F-F4).
DECLARE `s 76F(3) penalty` HAS
    `s 76F(3) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 76F(3) the longest imprisonment, in years` IS A NUMBER
    `s 76F(3) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:8978 | (3) Every director or chief executive officer of a company who
-- src:8979 | approves or authorises, the purchase or acquisition of the company’s
-- src:8980 | own shares or the release of obligations, knowing that the company is
-- src:8981 | not solvent shall, without affecting any other liability, be guilty of an
-- src:8982 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:8983 | $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years.
@ref s 76F(3) (src:8978-8983)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a chief executive officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person approves or authorises the purchase or acquisition of the company's own shares or the release of obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the company is not solvent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76F(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    (`the person is a director of the company` OR `the person is a chief executive officer of the company`)
      AND `the person approves or authorises the purchase or acquisition of the company's own shares or the release of obligations`
      AND `the person knows that the company is not solvent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i) of the brief, fork line F-F5): "Every director or chief executive officer of a company who approves or authorises, the purchase or acquisition of the company's own shares or the release of obligations, knowing that the company is not solvent shall ... be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts; it does not say the person is innocent of any other offence {F-F5} {MR-a}

-- src:8978 | (3) Every director or chief executive officer of a company who
