      `the person is a chief executive officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person approves or authorises the purchase or acquisition of the company's own shares or the release of obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the company is not solvent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 76F(3) penalty`
`s 76F(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 76F(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person is a director of the company` `the person is a chief executive officer of the company` `the person approves or authorises the purchase or acquisition of the company's own shares or the release of obligations` `the person knows that the company is not solvent` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 76F(3) penalty` OF 100000, 3, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty; the fine and the imprisonment are alternatives ("or"), so the court may not impose both under it (fork F-F4) {F-F4}

-- The prohibition derived from the offence (ruling N2 of 2026-11-04: where the text names the bearer, SHANT is derived). The bearer is "every director or chief executive officer".
DECLARE `s 76F act` IS ONE OF
    `s 76F(3) approve or authorise the purchase or acquisition of the company's own shares or the release of obligations, knowing that the company is not solvent`

